{"id":"mahabharata-7-164","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":164,"title":"चतुःषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 164 · The Brahmastra and the sages' warning","summary":{"en":"Drona, hurling Brahmastra, slaughters the Pandava army in thousands, and Duryodhana urges him on to destroy the Panchalas. Krishna sees that Drona cannot be conquered in open fight and advises Yudhishthira that he must be made to lay down arms by the false news of Ashvatthaman's death.","kn":"ದ್ರೋಣ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಾಸ್ತ್ರದಿಂದ ಸಾವಿರಾರು ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನಿಕರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಪಾಂಚಾಲರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡಲು ಅವನನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದ್ರೋಣನನ್ನು ನೇರ ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾಗದೆಂದು ಕಂಡ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಸತ್ತನೆಂಬ ಸುಳ್ಳು ಸುದ್ದಿಯಿಂದ ಆಯುಧ ಕೆಳಗಿಡಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रोण ब्रह्मास्त्र से हज़ारों पाण्डव सैनिकों का संहार करते हैं, और दुर्योधन उन्हें पाञ्चालों का नाश करने को उकसाता है। कृष्ण देखते हैं कि द्रोण खुले युद्ध में अजेय हैं और युधिष्ठिर को सलाह देते हैं कि अश्वत्थामा की मृत्यु की झूठी खबर से उन्हें शस्त्र रखवाना होगा।","te":"ద్రోణుడు బ్రహ్మాస్త్రంతో వేల పాండవ సైనికులను చంపుతాడు; పాంచాలులను నాశనం చేయమని దుర్యోధనుడు అతన్ని పురికొల్పుతాడు. ద్రోణుని బహిరంగ యుద్ధంలో గెలవలేమని చూసిన కృష్ణుడు అశ్వత్థామ మరణవార్త అనే అబద్ధంతో ఆయనను ఆయుధాలు వదిలేలా చేయాలని యుధిష్ఠిరునికి సలహా ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"த்ரோணர் பிரம்மாஸ்திரத்தால் ஆயிரக்கணக்கான பாண்டவ வீரரைக் கொல்ல, பாஞ்சாலரை அழிக்கும்படி துரியோதனன் அவரைத் தூண்டுகிறான். த்ரோணரை நேரடிப் போரில் வெல்ல முடியாது என்று கண்ட கண்ணன், அஸ்வத்தாமன் இறந்தான் என்ற பொய்ச்செய்தியால் அவரை ஆயுதம் துறக்கச் செய்யவேண்டும் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ബ്രഹ്മാസ്ത്രം പ്രയോഗിച്ച് ദ്രോണർ പാണ്ഡവ സേനയെ ആയിരക്കണക്കിന് കൊന്നൊടുക്കുന്നു; പാഞ്ചാലരെ നശിപ്പിക്കാൻ ദുര്യോധനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പ്രേരിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. തുറന്ന യുദ്ധത്തിൽ ദ്രോണരെ കീഴടക്കാനാവില്ലെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ കാണുന്നു; അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് മരിച്ചെന്ന വ്യാജവാർത്തകൊണ്ട് ആയുധം താഴെവെപ്പിക്കണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.164; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणवधपर्व","titleEn":"Dronavadha Parva (Slaying of Drona)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा वर्तमाने नराश्वगजसंक्षये ।\nदुःशासनो महाराज धृष्टद्युम्नमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that battle went on, destroying men, horses and elephants, Duhshasana, O great king, fought Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":2,"text":"स तु रुक्मरथासक्तो दुःशासनशरार्दितः ।\nअमर्षात्तव पुत्रस्य शरैर्वाहानवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, riding his golden chariot and wounded by Duhshasana's arrows, grew impatient and covered your son's horses with arrows."}},{"n":3,"text":"क्षणेन स रथस्तस्य सध्वजः सहसारथिः ।\nनादृश्यत महाराज पार्षतस्य शरैश्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In an instant that chariot of his, with its banner and charioteer, could not be seen, heaped over with the arrows of Prishata's son, O great king."}},{"n":4,"text":"दुःशासनस्तु राजेन्द्र पाञ्चाल्यस्य महात्मनः ।\nनाशकत्प्रमुखे स्थातुं शरजालप्रपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana, O king of kings, pressed by nets of arrows, could not stand before the great-souled Panchala."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तु दुःशासनं बाणैर्विमुखीकृत्य पार्षतः ।\nकिरञ्शरसहस्राणि द्रोणमेवाभ्ययाद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, turning Duhshasana away with arrows, pressed on toward Drona in the battle, scattering thousands of shafts."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रत्यपद्यत हार्दिक्यः कृतवर्मा तदन्तरम् ।\nसोदर्याणां त्रयश्चैव त एनं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarman, son of Hridika, took that opening, and three of your sons' brothers surrounded Dhrishtadyumna too."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं यमौ पृष्ठतोऽन्वैतां रक्षन्तौ पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nद्रोणायाभिमुखं यान्तं दीप्यमानमिवानलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twins, those two bulls among men, followed him from behind to protect him as he went blazing like fire toward Drona."}},{"n":8,"text":"संप्रहारमकुर्वंस्ते सर्वे सप्त महारथाः ।\nअमर्षिताः सत्त्ववन्तः कृत्वा मरणमग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All seven great chariot-warriors joined battle, impatient and brave, having resolved to meet death."}},{"n":9,"text":"शुद्धात्मानः शुद्धवृत्ता राजन्स्वर्गपुरस्कृताः ।\nआर्यं युद्धमकुर्वन्त परस्परजिगीषवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pure-hearted and pure in conduct, O king, with heaven set before them, they fought a noble fight, each wishing to conquer the other."}},{"n":10,"text":"शुक्लाभिजनकर्माणो मतिमन्तो जनाधिपाः ।\nधर्मयुद्धमयुध्यन्त प्रेक्षन्तो गतिमुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those kings of pure lineage and deeds, wise men, fought a righteous fight, looking to the highest goal."}},{"n":11,"text":"न तत्रासीदधर्मिष्ठमशस्त्रं युद्धमेव च ।\nनात्र कर्णी न नालीको न लिप्तो न च वस्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was no unrighteous fighting there, no use of weapons not allowed: no karni arrows, no nalika, no smeared or goat's-horn arrows,"}},{"n":12,"text":"न सूची कपिशो नात्र न गवास्थिर्गजास्थिकः ।\nइषुरासीन्न संश्लिष्टो न पूतिर्न च जिह्मगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"no needle-shafts, no tawny ones, no cow-bone or elephant-bone arrows. No shaft was crooked or rotten or bent."}},{"n":13,"text":"ऋजून्येव विशुद्धानि सर्वे शस्त्राण्यधारयन् ।\nसुयुद्धेन पराँल्लोकानीप्सन्तः कीर्तिमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They all carried straight and clean weapons, wishing for worlds beyond and for fame by a good fight."}},{"n":14,"text":"तदासीत्तुमुलं युद्धं सर्वदोषविवर्जितम् ।\nचतुर्णां तव योधानां तैस्त्रिभिः पाण्डवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"So a tumultuous battle took place, free of all fault, between four of your warriors and those three Pandavas."}},{"n":15,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तु तान्हित्वा तव राजन्रथर्षभान् ।\nयमाभ्यां वारितान्दृष्ट्वा शीघ्रास्त्रो द्रोणमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Dhrishtadyumna, quick with weapons, leaving your chariot heroes when he saw them held back by the twins, went on to Drona."}},{"n":16,"text":"निवारितास्तु ते वीरास्तयोः पुरुषसिंहयोः ।\nसमसज्जन्त चत्वारो वाताः पर्वतयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Held back by those two lions among men, those four heroes clashed like four winds against two mountains."}},{"n":17,"text":"द्वाभ्यां द्वाभ्यां यमौ सार्धं रथाभ्यां रथपुंगवौ ।\nसमासक्तौ ततो द्रोणं धृष्टद्युम्नोऽभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twins, bulls among charioteers, were each engaged with two chariots, and Dhrishtadyumna turned to Drona."}},{"n":18,"text":"दृष्ट्वा द्रोणाय पाञ्चाल्यं व्रजन्तं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nयमाभ्यां तांश्च संसक्तांस्तदन्तरमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Panchala heading for Drona, intoxicated with fighting, and those four locked with the twins, Duryodhana rushed into the gap."}},{"n":19,"text":"दुर्योधनो महाराज किरञ्शोणितभोजनान् ।\nतं सात्यकिः शीघ्रतरं पुनरेवाभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scattering blood-drinking arrows, O great king, he was met again swiftly by Satyaki."}},{"n":20,"text":"तौ परस्परमासाद्य समीपे कुरुमाधवौ ।\nहसमानौ नृशार्दूलावभीतौ समगच्छताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming close to each other, those two tigers among men, the Kuru and the Madhava, met fearless, smiling."}},{"n":21,"text":"बाल्ये वृत्तानि सर्वाणि प्रीयमाणौ विचिन्त्य तौ ।\nअन्योन्यं प्रेक्षमाणौ च हसमानौ पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Delighted, they both recalled all that had happened in their childhood, and looked at each other and laughed again and again."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथ दुर्योधनो राजा सात्यकिं प्रत्यभाषत ।\nप्रियं सखायं सततं गर्हयन्वृत्तमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana spoke to Satyaki, his dear friend, condemning his own conduct."}},{"n":23,"text":"धिक्क्रोधं धिक्सखे लोभं धिङ्मोहं धिगमर्षितम् ।\nधिगस्तु क्षात्रमाचारं धिगस्तु बलमौरसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said: Shame on anger, friend, shame on greed, shame on delusion, shame on impatience, shame on the kshatriya way, shame on physical strength!"}},{"n":24,"text":"यत्त्वं मामभिसंधत्से त्वां चाहं शिनिपुंगव ।\nत्वं हि प्राणैः प्रियतरो ममाहं च सदा तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since you aim at me and I at you, bull of the Shini line, though you are dearer to me than life, and I always to you."}},{"n":25,"text":"स्मरामि तानि सर्वाणि बाल्ये वृत्तानि यानि नौ ।\nतानि सर्वाणि जीर्णानि सांप्रतं नौ रणाजिरे ।\nकिमन्यत्क्रोधलोभाभ्यां युध्यामि त्वाद्य सात्वत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I remember all that happened to us in childhood. All of it has now grown old on this battlefield. What else but anger and greed makes me fight you today, Satvata?"}},{"n":26,"text":"तं तथावादिनं राजन्सात्यकिः प्रत्यभाषत ।\nप्रहसन्विशिखांस्तीक्ष्णानुद्यम्य परमास्त्रवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"To him speaking so, O king, Satyaki, skilled in the supreme weapons, replied, laughing and raising sharp arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"नेयं सभा राजपुत्र न चाचार्यनिवेशनम् ।\nयत्र क्रीडितमस्माभिस्तदा राजन्समागतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki said: This is not the assembly hall, king's son, nor the teacher's house, where we played as boys when we met together then, O king."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"क्व सा क्रीडा गतास्माकं बाल्ये वै शिनिपुंगव ।\nक्व च युद्धमिदं भूयः कालो हि दुरतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where has that play of ours in childhood gone, bull of the Shini line, and where is this fight again? Time is hard to overcome."}},{"n":29,"text":"किं नु नो विद्यते कृत्यं धनेन धनलिप्सया ।\nयत्र युध्यामहे सर्वे धनलोभात्समागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What need have we of wealth, from greed for riches, that we all gather here and fight for the sake of wealth?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"तं तथावादिनं तत्र राजानं माधवोऽब्रवीत् ।\nएवंवृत्तं सदा क्षत्रं यद्धन्तीह गुरूनपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"To the king speaking so, Madhava replied: This is always the way of the kshatriya, that he kills even his elders here."}},{"n":31,"text":"यदि तेऽहं प्रियो राजञ्जहि मां मा चिरं कृथाः ।\nत्वत्कृते सुकृताँल्लोकान्गच्छेयं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I am dear to you, king, kill me, do not delay. By your doing may I go to the worlds of the righteous, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":32,"text":"या ते शक्तिर्बलं चैव तत्क्षिप्रं मयि दर्शय ।\nनेच्छाम्येतदहं द्रष्टुं मित्राणां व्यसनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Show me at once whatever strength and power you have. I do not wish to see this great misfortune of my friends."}},{"n":33,"text":"इत्येवं व्यक्तमाभाष्य प्रतिभाष्य च सात्यकिः ।\nअभ्ययात्तूर्णमव्यग्रो निरपेक्षो विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so openly and replied, Satyaki went quickly forward, calm and indifferent, O lord of the people."}},{"n":34,"text":"तमायान्तमभिप्रेक्ष्य प्रत्यगृह्णात्तवात्मजः ।\nशरैश्चावाकिरद्राजञ्शैनेयं तनयस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come, your son met him and covered the Shini's grandson with arrows, O king."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं कुरुमाधवसिंहयोः ।\nअन्योन्यं क्रुद्धयोर्घोरं यथा द्विरदसिंहयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a fight began between the Kuru lion and the Madhava lion, each furious with the other, like that of an elephant and a lion."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः पूर्णायतोत्सृष्टैः सात्वतं युद्धदुर्मदम् ।\nदुर्योधनः प्रत्यविध्यद्दशभिर्निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with arrows loosed from a fully drawn bow, Duryodhana pierced Satyaki, who was drunk with battle, with ten sharp arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"तं सात्यकिः प्रत्यविध्यत्तथैव दशभिः शरैः ।\nपञ्चाशता पुनश्चाजौ त्रिंशता दशभिश्च ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki pierced him back with ten arrows in the same way, then with fifty, and again with thirty and with ten."}},{"n":38,"text":"तस्य संदधतश्चेषून्संहितेषुं च कार्मुकम् ।\nअच्छिनत्सात्यकिस्तूर्णं शरैश्चैवाभ्यवीवृषत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Duryodhana set arrows on his bow, Satyaki quickly cut the bow in two with its arrow and rained arrows on him."}},{"n":39,"text":"स गाढविद्धो व्यथितः प्रत्यपायाद्रथान्तरम् ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज दाशार्हशरपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply wounded and pained, Duryodhana withdrew into another chariot, O great king, tormented by the arrows of the Dasharha."}},{"n":40,"text":"समाश्वस्य तु पुत्रस्ते सात्यकिं पुनरभ्ययात् ।\nविसृजन्निषुजालानि युयुधानरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, recovered, went again against Satyaki, loosing nets of arrows at Yuyudhana's chariot."}},{"n":41,"text":"तथैव सात्यकिर्बाणान्दुर्योधनरथं प्रति ।\nप्रततं व्यसृजद्राजंस्तत्संकुलमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki too loosed unbroken arrows at Duryodhana's chariot, O king, and the fight was thick with them."}},{"n":42,"text":"तत्रेषुभिः क्षिप्यमाणैः पतद्भिश्च समन्ततः ।\nअग्नेरिव महाकक्षे शब्दः समभवन्महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With arrows flying and falling everywhere, a great noise arose, like fire in a huge dry thicket."}},{"n":43,"text":"तत्राभ्यधिकमालक्ष्य माधवं रथसत्तमम् ।\nक्षिप्रमभ्यपतत्कर्णः परीप्संस्तनयं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Madhava, best of charioteers, getting the better, Karna quickly rushed in to protect your son."}},{"n":44,"text":"न तु तं मर्षयामास भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nअभ्ययात्त्वरितः कर्णं विसृजन्सायकान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But mighty Bhima could not tolerate this, and hurried against Karna, loosing many arrows."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्य कर्णः शितान्बाणान्प्रतिहन्य हसन्निव ।\nधनुः शरांश्च चिच्छेद सूतं चाभ्यहनच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, as if laughing, knocked aside his sharp arrows, and cut Bhima's bow and arrows and struck his charioteer with arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु संक्रुद्धो गदामादाय पाण्डवः ।\nध्वजं धनुश्च सूतं च संममर्दाहवे रिपोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, enraged, took up his mace and crushed his enemy's banner, bow and charioteer in the battle."}},{"n":47,"text":"अमृष्यमाणः कर्णस्तु भीमसेनमयुध्यत ।\nविविधैरिषुजालैश्च नानाशस्त्रैश्च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, unable to bear it, fought Bhima in the battle with nets of arrows of many kinds and with many kinds of weapons."}},{"n":48,"text":"संकुले वर्तमाने तु राजा धर्मसुतोऽब्रवीत् ।\nपाञ्चालानां नरव्याघ्रान्मत्स्यानां च नरर्षभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that confusion went on, the king, son of Dharma, spoke to the tigers among men of the Panchalas and bulls among men of the Matsyas."}},{"n":49,"text":"ये नः प्राणाः शिरो ये नो ये नो योधा महाबलाः ।\nत एते धार्तराष्ट्रेषु विषक्ताः पुरुषर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said: Those who are our life, our head, our mighty warriors, those bulls among men, are entangled with Dhritarashtra's sons."}},{"n":50,"text":"किं तिष्ठत यथा मूढाः सर्वे विगतचेतसः ।\nतत्र गच्छत यत्रैते युध्यन्ते मामका रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why do you stand there like fools, all senseless? Go where these chariots of mine are fighting."}},{"n":51,"text":"क्षत्रधर्मं पुरस्कृत्य सर्व एव गतज्वराः ।\nजयन्तो वध्यमाना वा गतिमिष्टां गमिष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting the kshatriya duty first, all of you, free of fever of mind, you will win your wished-for goal, whether you win or are killed."}},{"n":52,"text":"जित्वा च बहुभिर्यज्ञैर्यक्ष्यध्वं भूरिदक्षिणैः ।\nहता वा देवसाद्भूत्वा लोकान्प्राप्स्यथ पुष्कलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you conquer, you will offer sacrifices with many gifts; if you are killed and become the gods', you will gain the fullest of worlds."}},{"n":53,"text":"ते राज्ञा चोदिता वीरा योत्स्यमाना महारथाः ।\nचतुर्धा वहिनीं कृत्वा त्वरिता द्रोणमभ्ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by the king, those heroes, great chariot-warriors, intent on fighting, divided their army in four and swiftly went against Drona."}},{"n":54,"text":"पाञ्चालास्त्वेकतो द्रोणमभ्यघ्नन्बहुभिः शरैः ।\nभीमसेनपुरोगाश्च एकतः पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas struck Drona from one side with many arrows, and those led by Bhima surrounded him from the other."}},{"n":55,"text":"आसंस्तु पाण्डुपुत्राणां त्रयोऽजिह्मा महारथाः ।\nयमौ च भीमसेनश्च प्राक्रोशन्त धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three upright great chariot-warriors of the Pandavas, the twins and Bhima, called out to Dhananjaya."}},{"n":56,"text":"अभिद्रवार्जुन क्षिप्रं कुरून्द्रोणादपानुद ।\nतत एनं हनिष्यन्ति पाञ्चाला हतरक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said: Rush, Arjuna, quickly, and drive the Kurus off from Drona. Then the Panchalas will kill him, with his guards gone."}},{"n":57,"text":"कौरवेयांस्ततः पार्थः सहसा समुपाद्रवत् ।\nपाञ्चालानेव तु द्रोणो धृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha suddenly rushed at the Kauravas, while Drona rushed at the Panchalas led by Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":58,"text":"पाञ्चालानां ततो द्रोणोऽप्यकरोत्कदनं महत् ।\nयथा क्रुद्धो रणे शक्रो दानवानां क्षयं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona then made a great slaughter among the Panchalas, as Indra in anger once did among the danavas."}},{"n":59,"text":"द्रोणास्त्रेण महाराज वध्यमानाः परे युधि ।\nनात्रसन्त रणे द्रोणात्सत्त्ववन्तो महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though struck by Drona's weapon in the battle, O great king, those courageous great chariot-warriors on the other side did not flinch from Drona."}},{"n":60,"text":"वध्यमाना महाराज पाञ्चालाः सृञ्जयास्तथा ।\nद्रोणमेवाभ्ययुर्युद्धे मोहयन्तो महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas and Srinjayas, being slain, O great king, still went against Drona in the fight, bewildering the great chariot-warrior."}},{"n":61,"text":"तेषां तूत्साद्यमानानां पाञ्चालानां समन्ततः ।\nअभवद्भैरवो नादो वध्यतां शरशक्तिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From those Panchalas, being destroyed on every side, as they were cut down by arrows and spears, a dreadful cry arose."}},{"n":62,"text":"वध्यमानेषु संग्रामे पाञ्चालेषु महात्मना ।\nउदीर्यमाणे द्रोणास्त्रे पाण्डवान्भयमाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Panchalas were killed in the battle by the great-souled one, and Drona's weapon spread, fear took hold of the Pandavas."}},{"n":63,"text":"दृष्ट्वाश्वनरसंघानां विपुलं च क्षयं युधि ।\nपाण्डवेया महाराज नाशंसुर्विजयं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the vast slaughter of horses, men and elephants in the battle, the Pandavas, O great king, did not hope for victory then."}},{"n":64,"text":"कच्चिद्द्रोणो न नः सर्वान्क्षपयेत्परमास्त्रवित् ।\nसमिद्धः शिशिरापाये दहन्कक्षमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They thought: Will Drona, knower of supreme weapons, not destroy us all, like a fire blazing in dry brush at the end of winter?"}},{"n":65,"text":"न चैनं संयुगे कश्चित्समर्थः प्रतिवीक्षितुम् ।\nन चैनमर्जुनो जातु प्रतियुध्येत धर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one in the battle could even look at him, and Arjuna, who knows dharma, would never fight him."}},{"n":66,"text":"त्रस्तान्कुन्तीसुतान्दृष्ट्वा द्रोणसायकपीडितान् ।\nमतिमाञ्श्रेयसे युक्तः केशवोऽर्जुनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the sons of Kunti terrified and tormented by Drona's arrows, wise Keshava, bent on their good, said to Arjuna:"}},{"n":67,"text":"नैष युद्धेन संग्रामे जेतुं शक्यः कथंचन ।\nअपि वृत्रहणा युद्धे रथयूथपयूथपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: He cannot be conquered by fighting in battle by any means, not even by Indra, the slayer of Vritra, the chief of the chiefs of chariot-warriors."}},{"n":68,"text":"आस्थीयतां जये योगो धर्ममुत्सृज्य पाण्डव ।\nयथा वः संयुगे सर्वान्न हन्याद्रुक्मवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Put aside dharma, son of Pandu, and resort to a device for victory, so that this man with the golden horses does not kill you all in the battle."}},{"n":69,"text":"अश्वत्थाम्नि हते नैष युध्येदिति मतिर्मम ।\nतं हतं संयुगे कश्चिदस्मै शंसतु मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think he would not fight if Ashvatthama were killed. Let some man tell him that Ashvatthama has been killed in the battle."}},{"n":70,"text":"एतन्नारोचयद्राजन्कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ।\nअन्ये त्वरोचयन्सर्वे कृच्छ्रेण तु युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, son of Kunti, did not approve this, O king. The others approved, and Yudhishthira with difficulty."}},{"n":71,"text":"ततो भीमो महाबाहुरनीके स्वे महागजम् ।\nजघान गदया राजन्नश्वत्थामानमित्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhima, in his own army, killed with his mace a great elephant named Ashvatthama, O king."}},{"n":72,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु सव्रीडमुपेत्य द्रोणमाहवे ।\nअश्वत्थामा हत इति शब्दमुच्चैश्चकार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, a little ashamed, went up to Drona in the fight and cried out loudly that Ashvatthama was dead."}},{"n":73,"text":"अश्वत्थामेति हि गजः ख्यातो नाम्ना हतोऽभवत् ।\nकृत्वा मनसि तं भीमो मिथ्या व्याहृतवांस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For an elephant famed by the name Ashvatthama had been killed. Keeping that in mind, Bhima spoke the false words then."}},{"n":74,"text":"भीमसेनवचः श्रुत्वा द्रोणस्तत्परमप्रियम् ।\nमनसा सन्नगात्रोऽभूद्यथा सैकतमम्भसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Bhima's words, most unwelcome, Drona's limbs went limp in his mind, like sand in water."}},{"n":75,"text":"शङ्कमानः स तन्मिथ्या वीर्यज्ञः स्वसुतस्य वै ।\nहतः स इति च श्रुत्वा नैव धैर्यादकम्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, doubting that it was false, knowing his own son's prowess, though he heard 'he is killed,' he did not tremble, for his steadiness."}},{"n":76,"text":"स लब्ध्वा चेतनां द्रोणः क्षणेनैव समाश्वसत् ।\nअनुचिन्त्यात्मनः पुत्रमविषह्यमरातिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Recovering his senses, Drona in an instant took heart again, thinking of his son, whom enemies could not withstand."}},{"n":77,"text":"स पार्षतमभिद्रुत्य जिघांसुर्मृत्युमात्मनः ।\nअवाकिरत्सहस्रेण तीक्ष्णानां कङ्कपत्रिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rushing at Prishata's son, wishing to bring about his own death, he covered him with a thousand sharp heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":78,"text":"तं वै विंशतिसाहस्राः पाञ्चालानां नरर्षभाः ।\nतथा चरन्तं संग्रामे सर्वतो व्यकिरञ्शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Twenty thousand bulls among the Panchalas covered him with arrows from every side as he moved so in the battle."}},{"n":79,"text":"ततः प्रादुष्करोद्द्रोणो ब्राह्ममस्त्रं परंतपः ।\nवधाय तेषां शूराणां पाञ्चालानाममर्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, scorcher of foes, in anger brought forth the Brahma weapon to kill those brave Panchalas."}},{"n":80,"text":"ततो व्यरोचत द्रोणो विनिघ्नन्सर्वसोमकान् ।\nशिरांस्यपातयच्चापि पाञ्चालानां महामृधे ।\nतथैव परिघाकारान्बाहून्कनकभूषणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona shone as he slew all the Somakas, and in that great battle he struck off the heads of the Panchalas and arms like iron bars, adorned with gold."}},{"n":81,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः समरे भारद्वाजेन पार्थिवाः ।\nमेदिन्यामन्वकीर्यन्त वातनुन्ना इव द्रुमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down in the battle by Bharadvaja's son, those kings lay scattered on the earth like trees knocked down by the wind."}},{"n":82,"text":"कुञ्जराणां च पततां हयौघानां च भारत ।\nअगम्यरूपा पृथिवी मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With falling elephants and masses of horses, O Bharata, the earth was impassable, a swamp of flesh and blood."}},{"n":83,"text":"हत्वा विंशतिसाहस्रान्पाञ्चालानां रथव्रजान् ।\nअतिष्ठदाहवे द्रोणो विधूमोऽग्निरिव ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed twenty thousand bands of Panchala chariot-warriors, Drona stood in the battle blazing like a smokeless fire."}},{"n":84,"text":"तथैव च पुनः क्रुद्धो भारद्वाजः प्रतापवान् ।\nवसुदानस्य भल्लेन शिरः कायादपाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again, enraged, the mighty son of Bharadvaja cut off Vasudana's head from his body with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":85,"text":"पुनः पञ्चशतान्मत्स्यान्षट्सहस्रांश्च सृञ्जयान् ।\nहस्तिनामयुतं हत्वा जघानाश्वायुतं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again he killed five hundred Matsyas and six thousand Srinjayas, and then ten thousand elephants, and then ten thousand horses."}},{"n":86,"text":"क्षत्रियाणामभावाय दृष्ट्वा द्रोणमवस्थितम् ।\nऋषयोऽभ्यागमंस्तूर्णं हव्यवाहपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Drona standing there for the ruin of the kshatriyas, the sages hurried there, led by Agni."}},{"n":87,"text":"विश्वामित्रो जमदग्निर्भारद्वाजोऽथ गौतमः ।\nवसिष्ठः कश्यपोऽत्रिश्च ब्रह्मलोकं निनीषवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishvamitra, Jamadagni, Bharadvaja, Gautama, Vasishtha, Kashyapa and Atri, wishing to lead him to the world of Brahma,"}},{"n":88,"text":"सिकताः पृश्नयो गर्गा बालखिल्या मरीचिपाः ।\nभृगवोऽङ्गिरसश्चैव सूक्ष्माश्चान्ये महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"also the Sikatas, Prishnis, Gargas, Balakhilyas, the Marichipas, the Bhrigus, the Angirases and other subtle great sages,"}},{"n":89,"text":"त एनमब्रुवन्सर्वे द्रोणमाहवशोभिनम् ।\nअधर्मतः कृतं युद्धं समयो निधनस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"all said to Drona, who shone in the fight: This battle has been fought unrighteously. The time of your death has come."}},{"n":90,"text":"न्यस्यायुधं रणे द्रोण समेत्यास्मानवस्थितान् ।\nनातः क्रूरतरं कर्म पुनः कर्तुं त्वमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lay down your weapon in the battle, Drona, and look to us who are here. You should not do again so cruel a deed."}},{"n":91,"text":"वेदवेदाङ्गविदुषः सत्यधर्मपरस्य च ।\nब्राह्मणस्य विशेषेण तवैतन्नोपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This does not suit you, learned in the Vedas and their branches, devoted to truth and dharma, and above all a brahmin."}},{"n":92,"text":"न्यस्यायुधममोघेषो तिष्ठ वर्त्मनि शाश्वते ।\nपरिपूर्णश्च कालस्ते वस्तुं लोकेऽद्य मानुषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lay down your weapon, you of unfailing arrows, and stay on the eternal path. Your time to live in this human world is now complete."}},{"n":93,"text":"इति तेषां वचः श्रुत्वा भीमसेनवचश्च तत् ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नं च संप्रेक्ष्य रणे स विमनाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing their words, and those of Bhima, and looking at Dhrishtadyumna, he became dispirited in the battle."}},{"n":94,"text":"स दह्यमानो व्यथितः कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nअहतं वा हतं वेति पप्रच्छ सुतमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning and pained, he asked Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, whether his own son was dead or not."}},{"n":95,"text":"स्थिरा बुद्धिर्हि द्रोणस्य न पार्थो वक्ष्यतेऽनृतम् ।\nत्रयाणामपि लोकानामैश्वर्यार्थे कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Drona's mind was steady that Partha would not tell a lie, not even for lordship over the three worlds."}},{"n":96,"text":"तस्मात्तं परिपप्रच्छ नान्यं कंचिद्विशेषतः ।\nतस्मिंस्तस्य हि सत्याशा बाल्यात्प्रभृति पाण्डवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"So he asked him and no one else especially, for from childhood he had trust in the Pandava's truthfulness."}},{"n":97,"text":"ततो निष्पाण्डवामुर्वीं करिष्यन्तं युधां पतिम् ।\nद्रोणं ज्ञात्वा धर्मराजं गोविन्दो व्यथितोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Govinda, seeing that Drona, lord of warriors, would leave the earth without Pandavas, spoke in distress to the king of dharma:"}},{"n":98,"text":"यद्यर्धदिवसं द्रोणो युध्यते मन्युमास्थितः ।\nसत्यं ब्रवीमि ते सेना विनाशं समुपैष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: If Drona fights on for half a day in his anger, I tell you truly, your army will be destroyed."}},{"n":99,"text":"स भवांस्त्रातु नो द्रोणात्सत्याज्ज्यायोऽनृतं भवेत् ।\nअनृतं जीवितस्यार्थे वदन्न स्पृश्यतेऽनृतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So save us from Drona. A lie is better than truth here. One who speaks a lie to save life is not touched by the lie."}},{"n":100,"text":"तयोः संवदतोरेवं भीमसेनोऽब्रवीदिदम् ।\nश्रुत्वैव तं महाराज वधोपायं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While those two were talking so, Bhima said this, having heard of the means to kill that great-souled man."}},{"n":101,"text":"गाहमानस्य ते सेनां मालवस्येन्द्रवर्मणः ।\nअश्वत्थामेति विख्यातो गजः शक्रगजोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said: As Drona was plunging into your army, there was an elephant named Ashvatthama, like Indra's elephant, belonging to Indravarman, king of Malava."}},{"n":102,"text":"निहतो युधि विक्रम्य ततोऽहं द्रोणमब्रुवम् ।\nअश्वत्थामा हतो ब्रह्मन्निवर्तस्वाहवादिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was killed in the battle by my prowess, and then I said to Drona, 'Ashvatthama is dead, brahmin; turn back from the battle.'"}},{"n":103,"text":"नूनं नाश्रद्दधद्वाक्यमेष मे पुरुषर्षभः ।\nस त्वं गोविन्दवाक्यानि मानयस्व जयैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely this best of men did not believe my word. So you, who wish for victory, honor Govinda's words."}},{"n":104,"text":"द्रोणाय निहतं शंस राजञ्शारद्वतीसुतम् ।\nत्वयोक्तो नैष युध्येत जातु राजन्द्विजर्षभः ।\nसत्यवान्हि नृलोकेऽस्मिन्भवान्ख्यातो जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell Drona, O king, that Sharadvati's son is dead. If you say so, that best of brahmins will never fight on. For you are famed in this world of men as truthful, O lord of the people."}},{"n":105,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा कृष्णवाक्यप्रचोदितः ।\nभावित्वाच्च महाराज वक्तुं समुपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, urged on by Krishna's speech and by what was bound to be, O great king, Yudhishthira set about to say it."}},{"n":106,"text":"तमतथ्यभये मग्नो जये सक्तो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअव्यक्तमब्रवीद्राजन्हतः कुञ्जर इत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sunk in fear of untruth and set on victory, Yudhishthira said indistinctly, 'The elephant is dead,' as he said it."}},{"n":107,"text":"तस्य पूर्वं रथः पृथ्व्याश्चतुरङ्गुल उत्तरः ।\nबभूवैवं तु तेनोक्ते तस्य वाहास्पृशन्महीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before this, his chariot had been four finger-breadths above the ground. But when he had said it, his horses touched the earth."}},{"n":108,"text":"युधिष्ठिरात्तु तद्वाक्यं श्रुत्वा द्रोणो महारथः ।\nपुत्रव्यसनसंतप्तो निराशो जीवितेऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that statement from Yudhishthira, the great chariot-warrior Drona, tormented by grief for his son, gave up hope of living."}},{"n":109,"text":"आगस्कृतमिवात्मानं पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ।\nऋषिवाक्यं च मन्वानः श्रुत्वा च निहतं सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Feeling guilty toward the great-souled Pandavas, remembering the sages' words, and hearing that his son was dead,"}},{"n":110,"text":"विचेताः परमोद्विग्नो धृष्टद्युम्नमवेक्ष्य च ।\nयोद्धुं नाशक्नुवद्राजन्यथापूर्वमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, senseless and greatly distressed, looked at Dhrishtadyumna and could not fight, O king, as he had before, subduer of enemies."}},{"n":111,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा परमोद्विग्नं शोकोपहतचेतसम् ।\nपाञ्चालराजस्य सुतो धृष्टद्युम्नः समाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him greatly distressed, his mind struck by grief, Dhrishtadyumna, son of the king of Panchala, rushed at him."}},{"n":112,"text":"य इष्ट्वा मनुजेन्द्रेण द्रुपदेन महामखे ।\nलब्धो द्रोणविनाशाय समिद्धाद्धव्यवाहनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the one obtained by Drupada, lord of men, from the blazing fire in a great sacrifice, for Drona's destruction."}},{"n":113,"text":"स धनुर्जैत्रमादाय घोरं जलदनिस्वनम् ।\nदृढज्यमजरं दिव्यं शरांश्चाशीविषोपमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking his victorious bow, dreadful, roaring like a cloud, with firm string, ageless and divine, and arrows like venomous snakes,"}},{"n":114,"text":"संदधे कार्मुके तस्मिञ्शरमाशीविषोपमम् ।\nद्रोणं जिघांसुः पाञ्चाल्यो महाज्वालमिवानलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Panchala set on his bow an arrow like a venomous snake, wishing to kill Drona, who was like a fire with great flames."}},{"n":115,"text":"तस्य रूपं शरस्यासीद्धनुर्ज्यामण्डलान्तरे ।\nद्योततो भास्करस्येव घनान्ते परिवेशिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The form of that arrow within the ring of the bowstring was like the sun glittering in a halo at the end of the rains."}},{"n":116,"text":"पार्षतेन परामृष्टं ज्वलन्तमिव तद्धनुः ।\nअन्तकालमिव प्राप्तं मेनिरे वीक्ष्य सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Prishata's son took up that bow, blazing as it seemed, the soldiers thought that the time of death had come."}},{"n":117,"text":"तमिषुं संहितं तेन भारद्वाजः प्रतापवान् ।\nदृष्ट्वामन्यत देहस्य कालपर्यायमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that arrow set to the bow, mighty Bharadvaja's son thought that the turn of time had come for his body."}},{"n":118,"text":"ततः स यत्नमातिष्ठदाचार्यस्तस्य वारणे ।\nन चास्यास्त्राणि राजेन्द्र प्रादुरासन्महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the teacher strove to ward it off, but his weapons did not appear to the great-souled man."}},{"n":119,"text":"तस्य त्वहानि चत्वारि क्षपा चैकास्यतो गता ।\nतस्य चाह्नस्त्रिभागेन क्षयं जग्मुः पतत्रिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Four days and one night of his command had passed, and by a third of the day his arrows were spent."}},{"n":120,"text":"स शरक्षयमासाद्य पुत्रशोकेन चार्दितः ।\nविविधानां च दिव्यानामस्त्राणामप्रसन्नताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His arrows exhausted, afflicted with grief for his son, and his divine weapons turned unwilling,"}},{"n":121,"text":"उत्स्रष्टुकामः शस्त्राणि विप्रवाक्याभिचोदितः ।\nतेजसा प्रेर्यमाणश्च युयुधे सोऽतिमानुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"wanting to lay down his weapons, urged by the words of the sages, and driven on by his own energy, he fought in a way beyond human."}},{"n":122,"text":"अथान्यत्स समादाय दिव्यमाङ्गिरसं धनुः ।\nशरांश्च ब्रह्मदण्डाभान्धृष्टद्युम्नमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he took up another divine bow of Angirasa's line and arrows bright as the staff of Brahma, and fought Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":123,"text":"ततस्तं शरवर्षेण महता समवाकिरत् ।\nव्यशातयच्च संक्रुद्धो धृष्टद्युम्नममर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he covered him with a great rain of arrows, and the angry Drona, impatient, struck at Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":124,"text":"तं शरं शतधा चास्य द्रोणश्चिच्छेद सायकैः ।\nध्वजं धनुश्च निशितैः सारथिं चाप्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona cut his arrow into a hundred pieces with shafts, and brought down his banner, bow and charioteer with sharp arrows."}},{"n":125,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः प्रहस्यान्यत्पुनरादाय कार्मुकम् ।\nशितेन चैनं बाणेन प्रत्यविध्यत्स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, laughing, took up another bow and pierced him between the breasts with a sharp arrow."}},{"n":126,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महेष्वासः संभ्रान्त इव संयुगे ।\nभल्लेन शितधारेण चिच्छेदास्य महद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply pierced, the great archer, as if confused in the battle, cut the other's great bow with a sharp-edged broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":127,"text":"यच्चास्य बाणं विकृतं धनूंषि च विशां पते ।\nसर्वं संछिद्य दुर्धर्षो गदां खड्गमथापि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever other arrows or bows he had, lord of the people, the unconquerable one cut them all, and his mace and sword also."}},{"n":128,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नं ततोऽविध्यन्नवभिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nजीवितान्तकरैः क्रुद्धः क्रुद्धरूपं परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the scorcher of foes, in anger, pierced the angry Dhrishtadyumna with nine sharp life-ending arrows."}},{"n":129,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नरथस्याश्वान्स्वरथाश्वैर्महारथः ।\nअमिश्रयदमेयात्मा ब्राह्ममस्त्रमुदीरयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warrior of immeasurable soul, invoking the Brahma weapon, mingled Dhrishtadyumna's horses with his own."}},{"n":130,"text":"ते मिश्रा बह्वशोभन्त जवना वातरंहसः ।\nपारावतसवर्णाश्च शोणाश्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those mixed horses, swift as the wind and pigeon-gray and red, shone greatly, O best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":131,"text":"यथा सविद्युतो मेघा नदन्तो जलदागमे ।\nतथा रेजुर्महाराज मिश्रिता रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"As clouds with lightning thunder at the coming of the rains, so they shone, mixed together at the head of the battle, great king."}},{"n":132,"text":"ईषाबन्धं चक्रबन्धं रथबन्धं तथैव च ।\nप्रणाशयदमेयात्मा धृष्टद्युम्नस्य स द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That brahmin of immeasurable soul destroyed the shaft-fastening, the wheel-fastening and the chariot-fastening of Dhrishtadyumna's chariot."}},{"n":133,"text":"स छिन्नधन्वा विरथो हताश्वो हतसारथिः ।\nउत्तमामापदं प्राप्य गदां वीरः परामृशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his bow cut, chariotless, his horses and charioteer slain, the hero, come into the greatest peril, took up a mace."}},{"n":134,"text":"तामस्य विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैः क्षिप्यमाणां महारथः ।\nनिजघान शरैर्द्रोणः क्रुद्धः सत्यपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it was being hurled at him, the great chariot-warrior Drona, angry and true in valor, struck it down with sharp arrows."}},{"n":135,"text":"तां दृष्ट्वा तु नरव्याघ्रो द्रोणेन निहतां शरैः ।\nविमलं खड्गमादत्त शतचन्द्रं च भानुमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his mace struck down by Drona's arrows, that tiger among men took up a bright sword and a shining shield with a hundred moons."}},{"n":136,"text":"असंशयं तथाभूते पाञ्चाल्यः साध्वमन्यत ।\nवधमाचार्यमुख्यस्य प्राप्तकालं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this plight, the Panchala surely thought rightly that the death of the foremost of teachers, the great-souled one, had come."}},{"n":137,"text":"ततः स्वरथनीडस्थः स्वरथस्य रथेषया ।\nअगच्छदसिमुद्यम्य शतचन्द्रं च भानुमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, standing in the seat of his own chariot, he went along the pole of his chariot with sword raised and the shield of a hundred moons, shining."}},{"n":138,"text":"चिकीर्षुर्दुष्करं कर्म धृष्टद्युम्नो महारथः ।\nइयेष वक्षो भेत्तुं च भारद्वाजस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warrior Dhrishtadyumna, wishing to do a hard deed, wished to pierce Bharadvaja's chest in the battle."}},{"n":139,"text":"सोऽतिष्ठद्युगमध्ये वै युगसंनहनेषु च ।\nशोणानां जघनार्धेषु तत्सैन्याः समपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He stood in the middle of the yoke, on the yoke-fastenings, and on the rear halves of the red horses, and his troops applauded."}},{"n":140,"text":"तिष्ठतो युगपालीषु शोणानप्यधितिष्ठतः ।\nनापश्यदन्तरं द्रोणस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he stood on the yoke-guards and even on the red horses, Drona could find no opening, and it was a marvel."}},{"n":141,"text":"क्षिप्रं श्येनस्य चरतो यथैवामिषगृद्धिनः ।\nतद्वदासीदभीसारो द्रोणं प्रार्थयतो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a hawk swiftly moves, greedy for meat, so was Dhrishtadyumna's attack as he sought Drona in the battle."}},{"n":142,"text":"तस्याश्वान्रथशक्त्यासौ तदा क्रुद्धः पराक्रमी ।\nसर्वानेकैकशो द्रोणः कपोताभानजीघनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the angry and valiant Drona struck all his horses, dove-gray, one by one with the chariot spear."}},{"n":143,"text":"ते हता न्यपतन्भूमौ धृष्टद्युम्नस्य वाजिनः ।\nशोणाश्च पर्यमुच्यन्त रथबन्धाद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck, those horses of Dhrishtadyumna fell to the ground, and the red horses were freed from the chariot's bonds, lord of the people."}},{"n":144,"text":"तान्हयान्निहतान्दृष्ट्वा द्विजाग्र्येण स पार्षतः ।\nनामृष्यत युधां श्रेष्ठो याज्ञसेनिर्महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those horses killed by the best of brahmins, the Panchala, son of Yajnasena, best of fighters, a great chariot-warrior, could not bear it."}},{"n":145,"text":"विरथः स गृहीत्वा तु खड्गं खड्गभृतां वरः ।\nद्रोणमभ्यपतद्राजन्वैनतेय इवोरगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariotless, taking up a sword, best of swordsmen, he fell on Drona, O king, like Vainateya on a serpent."}},{"n":146,"text":"तस्य रूपं बभौ राजन्भारद्वाजं जिघांसतः ।\nयथा रूपं परं विष्णोर्हिरण्यकशिपोर्वधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"His form, as he sought to kill Bharadvaja, shone like Vishnu's supreme form at the slaying of Hiranyakashipu."}},{"n":147,"text":"सोऽचरद्विविधान्मार्गान्प्रकारानेकविंशतिम् ।\nभ्रान्तमुद्भ्रान्तमाविद्धमाप्लुतं प्रसृतं सृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He moved in many paths and twenty-one ways: whirling, circling, thrusting, leaping, spreading and gliding,"}},{"n":148,"text":"परिवृत्तं निवृत्तं च खड्गं चर्म च धारयन् ।\nसंपातं समुदीर्णं च दर्शयामास पार्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"turning around and turning back, holding sword and shield, and Prishata's son showed his rushing in and his attack in full force."}},{"n":149,"text":"ततः शरसहस्रेण शतचन्द्रमपातयत् ।\nखड्गं चर्म च संबाधे धृष्टद्युम्नस्य स द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in that press Drona, the brahmin, cut Dhrishtadyumna's sword and shield, the one with a hundred moons, with a thousand arrows."}},{"n":150,"text":"ते तु वैतस्तिका नाम शरा ह्यासन्नघातिनः ।\nनिकृष्टयुद्धे द्रोणस्य नान्येषां सन्ति ते शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows, called vaitastikas, a span long, were deadly, and Drona alone had them in close fighting; others do not have such arrows."}},{"n":151,"text":"शारद्वतस्य पार्थस्य द्रौणेर्वैकर्तनस्य च ।\nप्रद्युम्नयुयुधानाभ्यामभिमन्योश्च ते शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such arrows belonged only to Sharadvata, Partha, Drona's son, Karna, Pradyumna, Yuyudhana and Abhimanyu."}},{"n":152,"text":"अथास्येषुं समाधत्त दृढं परमसंशितम् ।\nअन्तेवासिनमाचार्यो जिघांसुः पुत्रसंमितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the teacher set a firm, supremely sharpened arrow to his bow, wishing to kill his pupil as if he were his own son."}},{"n":153,"text":"तं शरैर्दशभिस्तीक्ष्णैश्चिच्छेद शिनिपुंगवः ।\nपश्यतस्तव पुत्रस्य कर्णस्य च महात्मनः ।\nग्रस्तमाचार्यमुख्येन धृष्टद्युम्नममोचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Shini line cut that arrow with ten sharp arrows, before your son and the great-souled Karna, and freed Dhrishtadyumna, who had been swallowed up by the chief of teachers."}},{"n":154,"text":"चरन्तं रथमार्गेषु सात्यकिं सत्यविक्रमम् ।\nद्रोणकर्णान्तरगतं कृपस्यापि च भारत ।\nअपश्येतां महात्मानौ विष्वक्सेनधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vishvaksena, Krishna, and Dhananjaya, the two great-souled ones, saw Satyaki, true in valor, moving on the chariot paths between Drona, Karna and Kripa, O Bharata."}},{"n":155,"text":"अपूजयेतां वार्ष्णेयं ब्रुवाणौ साधु साध्विति ।\nदिव्यान्यस्त्राणि सर्वेषां युधि निघ्नन्तमच्युतम् ।\nअभिपत्य ततः सेनां विष्वक्सेनधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They honored the Vrishni, saying 'Well done, well done!' as he, unwavering, struck down the divine weapons of all in the battle. Then they plunged into the army."}},{"n":156,"text":"धनंजयस्ततः कृष्णमब्रवीत्पश्य केशव ।\nआचार्यवरमुख्यानां मध्ये क्रीडन्मधूद्वहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhananjaya said to Krishna: See, Keshava, the bearer of Madhu's line playing among the best of teachers."}},{"n":157,"text":"आनन्दयति मां भूयः सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ च भीमं च राजानं च युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, true in valor, again delights me, and the sons of Madri, and Bhima and King Yudhishthira."}},{"n":158,"text":"यच्छिक्षयानुद्धतः सन्रणे चरति सात्यकिः ।\nमहारथानुपक्रीडन्वृष्णीनां कीर्तिवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through what he was taught, Satyaki goes about in the battle not proud, playing with great chariot-warriors, increasing the fame of the Vrishnis."}},{"n":159,"text":"तमेते प्रतिनन्दन्ति सिद्धाः सैन्याश्च विस्मिताः ।\nअजय्यं समरे दृष्ट्वा साधु साध्विति सात्वतम् ।\nयोधाश्चोभयतः सर्वे कर्मभिः समपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The siddhas and the astonished armies applaud him, seeing the Satvata invincible in battle with 'Well done, well done!' and all the warriors on both sides honored him for his deeds."}}]}]}